WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:55.260
<b>Reverse Mountain</b>

3
00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:19.540
But it seems to me
we're not even moving.

4
00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:20.700
You feel that?

5
00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:37.550
No! We're screwed!
We've entered the Calm Belt!

6
00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:38.890
The Clam Belt?

7
00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:39.720
What's that?

8
00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.530
Calm Belt!

9
00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.230
A part of the sea where
nothing moves a muscle!

10
00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:43.310
So there's mussels and clams?!

11
00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:44.520
No!

12
00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.610
What was that? An earthquake?

13
00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.400
A good trick since we're at sea.

14
00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.820
All of this chitchat isn't
going to get us outta here.

15
00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.740
Fold the sails and
start paddling now!

16
00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.330
We have to get back on course!

17
00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:01.700
You can count on me.

18
00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:03.790
Don't panic.

19
00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:05.540
And besides, this is a sailboat.
Why do we need to paddle?

20
00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:06.750
True.

21
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:07.760
And why would we go through
the trouble of doubling back

22
00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.590
when the Marines
are waiting for us?

23
00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:12.710
Look, there's no time to argue.
Just shut up and do as I say!

24
00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.550
At least it's nice
and quiet here.

25
00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:15.400
Ugh!

26
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.500
Fine! If I need to explain
it to you, I will!

27
00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.550
In our haste to escape
from the Marines,

28
00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:20.980
we ended up going too far south

29
00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.800
and now we're off course
and stuck out here.

30
00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.980
South? So we
entered the Grand Line?

31
00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.500
Woohoo!

32
00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:27.440
If we were at the Grand Line,

33
00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:29.860
you think I'd waste my
time explaining this?!

34
00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.440
Now look!

35
00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.900
The Grand Line is
sandwiched in the middle

36
00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.410
between these two green areas
you see here, ya understand?

37
00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:40.220
These areas, just
as they're labeled,

38
00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:41.830
are what's called
the Calm Belts.

39
00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:43.800
That's where we are!

40
00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:46.020
Nobody knows why,
but inside the Calm Belt,

41
00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:47.580
there's no wind and no current.

42
00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.630
It's like a void where
everything's stagnate.

43
00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:52.820
Given that sailboats move
by catching winds,

44
00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.130
this is more than a dangerous
region, it can be fatal!

45
00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:55.630
Get it?

46
00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.720
Nope, but it sounds
like we're in big trouble.

47
00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.180
Good. You retained more
than I thought you would.

48
00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.780
So this is what
that geezer meant

49
00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:04.770
when he said it was dangerous.

50
00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.130
Well that explains
why we haven't gotten

51
00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:07.270
a single gust of wind.

52
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.800
How're we gonna get outta this

53
00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.100
if our ship can't move?

54
00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.100
Maybe the wind'll
start blowing again.

55
00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.340
Wind never blows
in the Calm Belt!

56
00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.240
And that's not all.

57
00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.640
There's another good reason

58
00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:18.610
that people call this
area dangerous.

59
00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.030
It's infested with...

60
00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:21.890
Whoa!

61
00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:31.170
Sea Monsters! They're gigantic!

62
00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.590
The Calm Belt is also
home to the Sea Kings.

63
00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.550
It's their main place
for breeding.

64
00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:42.860
They're the biggest reason

65
00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:46.020
people can't cross
the Calm Belt.

66
00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:50.800
We don't wanna give
them any reason

67
00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:51.480
to stick around or eat us.

68
00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:54.860
Once they're gone,
we'll paddle back. Got it?

69
00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.610
You call that a plan?!

70
00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:57.490
Shut up!

71
00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:01.070
Sorry.

72
00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.160
That didn't improve anything!

73
00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.250
It sounds like it's gonna...

74
00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:09.260
Brace yourselves!

75
00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:11.120
I think this behemoth's
gonna sneeze!

76
00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.350
Oh, well, at least we're
back on our original course.

77
00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.740
According to the map,

78
00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.900
we should be spotting
the Red Line any time now.

79
00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:40.950
Wow! We're almost there!
The Grand Line, at last!

80
00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:42.720
Hehehe. Isn't this exciting?!

81
00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:46.030
We're finally going!
We did it! We did it!

82
00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.620
Cut it out!

83
00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:48.700
Sorry!

84
00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:50.830
Zoro! Can you believe it?!

85
00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:52.470
Can this be right?

86
00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:54.930
Is the path to the Grand Line
really as perilous

87
00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.230
as it's drawn here?

88
00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.420
Stop that!

89
00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.260
Hmm?

90
00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.140
Take a look!

91
00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:06.920
I'm familiar with the rumors,

92
00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:09.060
and these drawings confirm it!

93
00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:11.060
As unimaginable as it may seem,

94
00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:13.100
the entrance to the
Grand Line is a mountain!

95
00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.650
A mountain?!

96
00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:16.020
So what, do we crash into it?

97
00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.150
You gotta be kidding...

98
00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:19.860
I didn't believe it,
but the map's clear...

99
00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:22.150
The mountain appears to
be riddled with small canals,

100
00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:24.320
so we might have
to go up and over it.

101
00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.200
Ooo! Sounds like fun!

102
00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:28.660
What are you talking about...?!

103
00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:30.880
Even if there are
canals or whatever,

104
00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.040
a ship can't
climb up a mountain!

105
00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.670
Well, the map says otherwise!

106
00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:36.050
That's right!

107
00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:37.550
And if Nami thinks something
can be done, then it can!

108
00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:38.480
Got that?!

109
00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:39.850
Yeah, but remember
that map was stolen

110
00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:42.800
from Buggy the Clown...
So can we trust it?

111
00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:46.140
In case no one's
noticed, the rudder's stuck!

112
00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:48.510
Sanji! Will you
please give Usopp a hand?

113
00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:50.850
I can't think with
all his shouting!

114
00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.390
Right away, Nami!

115
00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:53.480
Okay!

116
00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:57.400
Uh, does this current seem
unusually strong to anyone else?

117
00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.770
Hmm? Usopp! What did
you just say?

118
00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.280
I asked if any of you noticed

119
00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:02.530
the insane strength
of this current!

120
00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:05.150
The current... That must be...

121
00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.280
What is it?

122
00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.120
The canals do go
up the mountain!

123
00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.660
Oh, come on... How could
that possibly work?

124
00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:11.370
Look right here!

125
00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.590
Ya see...? The guiding
light was directing us

126
00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:15.710
toward this spot
on the Red Line...

127
00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:18.040
Notice how it's labeled
here... Reverse Mountain!

128
00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.500
Hello...! Little help
over here, thank you!

129
00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.330
These green lines
represent canals,

130
00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.060
or artificial waterways...

131
00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:27.130
If major currents
from all four oceans

132
00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.330
flow toward this mountain,

133
00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.160
what do you
think's gonna happen?

134
00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:32.770
The currents would force
water up these canals,

135
00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.230
collide at the top,

136
00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:36.310
and then flow straight
down into the Grand Line!

137
00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:38.400
Now, Reverse Mountain
is a "winter mountain,"

138
00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:39.020
so it's cold, right?

139
00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:42.440
That means any surface currents
that don't flow up the canal

140
00:07:42.470 --> 00:07:44.190
will be forced
down as they cool.

141
00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:47.160
Anything riding those currents
would be pulled down as well.

142
00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:50.120
If we screw up and miss
the entrance to the canal,

143
00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:51.350
the Going Merry
will be carried straight

144
00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:53.460
into the Red Line's rock face

145
00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:55.600
and likely be destroyed.

146
00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:56.870
Ship and crew would be sucked

147
00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:58.250
to the bottom of
the sea. Understand?

148
00:07:58.250 --> 00:07:59.670
Yeah...

149
00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:02.710
Basically... it's a mystery
mountain! Ha. Ha. Ha.

150
00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:07.010
No, that's
not my point at all.

151
00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:09.360
Anyways, since we're
positioned on this current,

152
00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:10.920
we shouldn't run
into any problems

153
00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.960
getting to the summit
of Reverse Mountain!

154
00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:14.260
Only thing that
would hurt us now

155
00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.930
is if something went
wrong with the rudder.

156
00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:18.060
Nami, you're a genius...

157
00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:20.980
Call me a skeptic, but ships
do not climb mountains.

158
00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:22.690
Well, I've heard
a few stories...

159
00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:24.480
Stories about the
"mystery mountain"?

160
00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:25.690
No...

161
00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.530
What I have heard is that
more than half of the people

162
00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.160
who try to make it
to the Grand Line die

163
00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:30.700
before they even get there.

164
00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:34.740
Whatever we find,
it isn't going to be easy...

165
00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.620
Sanji! Could you get the sail?

166
00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:38.370
Anything for you, Nami!

167
00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:39.500
Luffy! Help me!

168
00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:44.590
Got it!

169
00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:55.350
Hey...! I can see the
"mystery mountain"!

170
00:08:55.350 --> 00:09:00.020
Aaah! That's insanely huge!

171
00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:04.980
Haha! Oh, wow! Awesome!
It's bigger than I thought!

172
00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:07.300
I can't see the top!

173
00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:11.490
It's taller than the clouds!

174
00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:33.720
We're getting sucked in!

175
00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:35.970
Hold the rudder steady!

176
00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:37.470
– We're on it!
– We're on it!

177
00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.360
Where's that entrance
you were talking about?!

178
00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:50.320
If we keep this heading, we're
gonna crash into the rocks!

179
00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:54.390
There's a crack in that cliff...

180
00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:56.590
That must be it.

181
00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:00.290
Nami...! Give us a direction!

182
00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:01.710
Keep bearing straight ahead!

183
00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:02.870
You can't be serious!

184
00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.080
Trust me!

185
00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:05.700
Have we made it?

186
00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:07.040
Is that the canal entrance?

187
00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.500
More than likely!

188
00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.970
I've gotta be dreaming!

189
00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:13.140
It's impossible...

190
00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:17.210
The ocean really is
flowing up the mountain!

191
00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:20.870
We have to make our way

192
00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:23.480
through those water
gates just right.

193
00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:26.360
Or we'll crash into the Red Line
and be smashed to pieces...

194
00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:31.190
We're drifting off course!

195
00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:33.360
Gotta go more
to the right! Right!

196
00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:35.660
The right?! Move it starboard!

197
00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.950
Come on, now!
Put your back into it!

198
00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:49.420
– The rudder!
– The rudder!

199
00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:52.130
Gum-Gum Balloon!

200
00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:02.310
Luffy!

201
00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:03.180
Grab ahold!

202
00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:15.500
Yeah! Yeah! Yay!

203
00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:18.740
– We made it!
– We made it!

204
00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:28.210
Now it's just a straight
shot to the summit!

205
00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:43.560
Whoa! Look how high we are!

206
00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.440
We're in the clouds!

207
00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:01.700
This is insane!

208
00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:05.200
We're not in the clouds,
we're above them!

209
00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:16.810
It's amazing... We've done it!

210
00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:18.630
We've reached the summit!

211
00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:33.650
Wh-hoo!

212
00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.710
Hahahaha!

213
00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:55.800
I can see it!

214
00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:58.630
This is the greatest sea
in the whole world!

215
00:12:58.630 --> 00:12:59.930
The Grand Line!

216
00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:04.610
Somewhere out there
the One Piece is waiting,

217
00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:06.970
and we're gonna find it!

218
00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:10.100
Let's go!

219
00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:26.490
Did you guys just
hear something?

220
00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:28.410
It was probably just the wind!

221
00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:31.580
At this speed everything
sounds distorted!

222
00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.210
What was that?

223
00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:40.300
Nami! I see a mountain up ahead!

224
00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:42.630
What? That's impossible...

225
00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.680
But it's right
there! I can see it!

226
00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:46.970
Who cares...?! Go!

227
00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.420
After we pass
the Twin Capes up ahead,

228
00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:51.640
there should be
nothing but ocean!

229
00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:53.620
Hmm?

230
00:13:57.250 --> 00:14:02.220
Aaaaah!

231
00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:03.740
It's a black wall!

232
00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:04.910
No, it's not!

233
00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:06.030
Then, what is it?!

234
00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:08.840
It's a whale!

235
00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:14.100
What are we gonna do?!

236
00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:14.990
Should we fight?

237
00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:16.260
Idiot! How are
we supposed

238
00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:17.180
to fight a 100-ton whale?!

239
00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:18.950
B-B-B-B-But, we
h-h-have to do something!

240
00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:21.220
Our path is blocked!
How do we escape?!

241
00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:22.670
Calm down!

242
00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:25.190
If this creature looks
like a giant wall to us,

243
00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.180
we must be a spec!

244
00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:28.000
That's right...!

245
00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:29.500
It's highly possible
that this thing

246
00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:31.310
isn't even aware
that we're here!

247
00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:33.850
We'll run right into
it unless we change course!

248
00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:35.900
Look... We can
get by on the left!

249
00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:38.360
Port...! Hard to port!

250
00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.440
The rudder's broken!

251
00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:42.900
Do something! Anything!

252
00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:44.280
Wait...! I know!

253
00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:46.570
This'll work! It has to!

254
00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:47.240
Hey!

255
00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.120
Luffy, what're you doing?!

256
00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:56.290
This is pointless!

257
00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.880
The ship's not gonna turn!

258
00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.170
Dammit!

259
00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.300
Don't give up!

260
00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:12.890
Is this the end?!

261
00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:22.110
– The cannon?!
– The cannon?!

262
00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:24.070
Done...

263
00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:28.490
Someone's coming out.

264
00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:33.160
We're screwed...

265
00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:34.580
